# Instructions

During your interaction with the user, if you find anything reusable in this project (e.g. version of a library, model name), especially about a fix to a mistake you made or a correction you received, you should take note in the `Lessons` section in the `.cursorrules` file so you will not make the same mistake again.

You should also use the `.cursorrules` file as a Scratchpad to organize your thoughts. Especially when you receive a new task, you should first review the content of the Scratchpad, clear old different task if necessary, first explain the task, and plan the steps you need to take to complete the task. You can use todo markers to indicate the progress, e.g.
[X] Task 1
[ ] Task 2

Also update the progress of the task in the Scratchpad when you finish a subtask.

# Tools

Note all the tools are in python3. Consult `tools/` for screenshot, search, scrape, and LLM helpers.

# Lessons

- War section charts must stay centered with `mx-auto w-full max-w-*`; do not use `w-screen left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2` inside the RTL report frame because it can shift beyond the artboard.
- Vite build-html treats `href="/"` or `content="/"` in index.html as asset URLs (EISDIR). Keep root canonical/og:url out of source index.html; inject absolute URLs in postbuild (`scripts/generate-seo-static.mjs`).
- Persian year/day comparisons must use an explicit 3-column RTL grid (`date | date`) with each date rendered as one uninterrupted RTL string. Nested flex/bidi isolation produced no reliable visual change.
- Both reports must render without international internet. Runtime fonts are the tracked files in `public/fonts`; do not restore Google Fonts or other external CSS/script/image requests. Schema.org/XML namespace URLs are identifiers, not network dependencies.

## Scratchpad

